	url = {https://linkinghub.elsevier.com/retrieve/pii/S1474034625009644},
	doi = {10.1016/j.aei.2025.104071},
	abstract = {With the increasing demands and conditions placed on the unmanned aerial vehicle (UAV) in real-world applications, UAV path planning has gradually become a key factor affecting task execution efficiency, requiring more efficient algorithms to solve related models. In recent years, the nature inspired algorithm (NIA) have been widely improved and applied to engineering examples in many fields due to its advantages of simple use and significant optimization ability. Therefore, this article proposes a multi strategy particle swarm optimization to solve the smooth coverage path planning model of the UAV group, and introduces obstacles with more shapes in the simulated environment. To provide the UAV group with more free flight trajectories, this paper introduces the G2 connected Said-Ball curve (SBC) and designs multiple necessary points as endpoints of the polynomial curve. Firstly, this article establishes a smooth coverage path planning model for the UAV group containing six constraint conditions. Secondly, ACDMRPSO is proposed by introducing adaptive quadratic interpolation strategy, crossover sexual cannibalism strategy, dual lens fusion enhanced opposition-based learning strategy, mutation evolution population dynamics strategy, and restart integer conversion strategy into the basic particle swarm optimization. Then, the better comprehensive performance of ACDMRPSO is verified through population diversity analysis, ablation analysis, and dimensional sensitivity analysis, and the mean rank of ACDMRPSO achieves the first place in 18 out of 30 benchmark experiments. Finally, in three sets of simulation experiments with different types of obstacles and shapes of the walls to be detected, the optimal path found by ACDMRPSO is more in line with the constraint requirements than the other five algorithms that rank high in comprehensive performance in the benchmark experiments, and it ranks first in four performance indicators in 83.3\% of the three scenarios. ACDMRPSO can always provide a smoother and higher coverage flight path for the UAV group, which proves that it can provide more effective solutions for both benchmark experiments and UAV path planning models.},
	language = {en},
